## UI Craft: sticky section sub-bar with sliding active pill

Stack: css-handoff (UX_DESIGNER, CSS only) · Theme: light + dark · States: complete

I assumed defaults because this is a single component, so the cold-start question is skipped. There is no `design/` folder in the project. If `design/tokens.css` is added later, delete the token block and link that file. I did not check the CSS in a browser. The contrast figures come from the colour values, not from a rendered page.

### Tokens and architecture
- The default `design-system` token names are used, so the block is easy to swap out later.
- Light is the default. Dark follows `[data-theme="dark"]`, or `prefers-color-scheme` unless `data-theme="light"` is set.
- The `--z-*` scale uses the exact names `--z-sticky`, `--z-dropdown`, `--z-command`, `--z-modal` and `--z-toast`.
- The bar uses a 4px grid, `--r-*` radii and 44px tap targets.
- The glass background has an opaque fallback inside `@supports not (backdrop-filter…)`.
- The pill sits behind the tabs and moves with `transform: translateX()`. Its width is set per tab and animated, as `references/navigation-and-states.md` specifies.
- The tab track scrolls sideways inside the bar, so the page never gets horizontal overflow at 390px.
- The contrast figures below are approximate, calculated from the hex values:

| Pair | Contrast |
|---|---|
| Muted text on `--color-surface-subtle` | about 6.9:1 (light) |
| Muted text on `--color-surface-subtle` | about 7:1 (dark) |
| Default text on the pill | well above 4.5:1 |

### Code: `subbar.css`
```css
/* ===== Tokens (default block, same names as design-system) ===== */
:root {
  color-scheme: light dark;
  --color-surface-default: #ffffff;
  --color-surface-raised: #fafafa;
  --color-surface-subtle: #f4f4f5;
  --glass-blur: 20px;
  --glass-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface-raised) 74%, transparent);
  --color-text-default: #09090b;
  --color-text-muted: #52525b;
  --color-border-default: #e4e4e7;
  --color-border-strong: #a1a1aa;
  --color-border-focus: #2563eb;
  --shadow-1: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  --shadow-2: 0 8px 24px -8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  --r-xs: 4px;
  --r-sm: 6px;
  --r-md: 10px;
  --r-lg: 14px;
  --r-xl: 16px;
  --z-base: 1;
  --z-sticky: 20;
  --z-dropdown: 40;
  --z-command: 60;
  --z-modal: 80;
  --z-toast: 100;
  --line-height-khmer: 1.6;
}

:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  --color-surface-default: #09090b;
  --color-surface-raised: #121216;
  --color-surface-subtle: #1c1c22;
  --glass-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface-raised) 78%, transparent);
  --color-text-default: #fafafa;
  --color-text-muted: #a1a1aa;
  --color-border-default: #27272a;
  --color-border-strong: #52525b;
  --color-border-focus: #60a5fa;
  --shadow-2: 0 10px 28px -8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --color-surface-default: #09090b;
    --color-surface-raised: #121216;
    --color-surface-subtle: #1c1c22;
    --glass-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface-raised) 78%, transparent);
    --color-text-default: #fafafa;
    --color-text-muted: #a1a1aa;
    --color-border-default: #27272a;
    --color-border-strong: #52525b;
    --color-border-focus: #60a5fa;
    --shadow-2: 0 10px 28px -8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  }
}

:lang(km) {
  line-height: var(--line-height-khmer);
  letter-spacing: 0;
}

/* ===== Sticky section sub-bar ===== */
.subbar {
  /* Engineering may set --subbar-top to the height of any fixed main header. */
  --subbar-top: 0px;
  --subbar-ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  position: sticky;
  top: var(--subbar-top);
  z-index: var(--z-sticky);
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1120px;
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding: 4px 8px;
  background: var(--color-surface-raised); /* opaque fallback */
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
  transition: box-shadow 160ms var(--subbar-ease), border-color 160ms var(--subbar-ease);
}

@supports (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
  .subbar {
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(140%);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(140%);
  }
}

.subbar[data-scrolled="true"] {
  border-bottom-color: var(--color-border-strong);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-2);
}

/* Track scrolls sideways inside the bar, never the page. */
.subbar__track {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 4px;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
  scrollbar-width: none;
  isolation: isolate; /* keeps the pill's z-index: -1 inside the track */
}
.subbar__track::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }

/* Sliding pill: engineering sets --pill-x and --pill-w. */
.subbar__pill {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  z-index: -1;
  width: var(--pill-w, 0px);
  transform: translateX(var(--pill-x, 0px));
  background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
  border-radius: var(--r-sm);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  transition:
    transform 220ms var(--subbar-ease),
    width 220ms var(--subbar-ease),
    opacity 120ms linear;
}
.subbar[data-ready="true"] .subbar__pill { opacity: 1; }

/* Tabs */
.subbar__link {
  position: relative;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--r-sm);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  font: inherit;
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.5;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-decoration: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: color 120ms linear, transform 120ms var(--subbar-ease);
}

.subbar__link:hover {
  color: var(--color-text-default);
  border-color: var(--color-border-strong);
}
.subbar__link:active { transform: translateY(1px); }

.subbar__link:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-border-focus);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.subbar__link[aria-current="true"],
.subbar__link[aria-current="location"],
.subbar__link[aria-current="page"] {
  color: var(--color-text-default);
  font-weight: 500;
  border-color: transparent; /* the pill draws the border */
}
.subbar__link[aria-current]:hover { border-color: transparent; }

.subbar__link[aria-disabled="true"],
.subbar__link:disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.subbar__count {
  margin-inline-start: 8px;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

/* Fallback when there is no JS: the active tab draws its own pill. */
.subbar:not([data-ready="true"]) .subbar__link[aria-current] {
  background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
  border-color: var(--color-border-default);
}

/* Loading state: fixed-size placeholders so there is no layout shift. */
.subbar[aria-busy="true"] .subbar__link {
  color: transparent;
  pointer-events: none;
  background: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    var(--color-surface-subtle) 25%,
    var(--color-border-default) 50%,
    var(--color-surface-subtle) 75%
  );
  background-size: 200% 100%;
  animation: subbar-shimmer 1.2s linear infinite;
}
.subbar[aria-busy="true"] .subbar__pill { opacity: 0; }
@keyframes subbar-shimmer {
  from { background-position: 200% 0; }
  to   { background-position: -200% 0; }
}

/* Empty (no sections) and error (with retry) */
.subbar__empty,
.subbar__error {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0 12px;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
.subbar__error[role="alert"] {
  color: var(--color-danger-text, #b91c1c);
  background: var(--color-danger-bg-subtle, #fef2f2);
  border-radius: var(--r-sm);
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .subbar__error[role="alert"] {
  --color-danger-text: #f87171;
  --color-danger-bg-subtle: rgba(185, 28, 28, 0.16);
}
.subbar__retry {
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--r-sm);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--color-text-default);
  font: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.subbar__retry:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-border-focus);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* Anchor targets must clear the sticky bar. */
[data-subbar-target] { scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--subbar-top, 0px) + 64px); }

/* Narrow screens */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .subbar { padding: 4px; }
  .subbar__link { padding: 0 12px; }
}

/* Reduced motion: no sliding, but the active state is still clear. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .subbar,
  .subbar__pill,
  .subbar__link { transition: none; }
  .subbar[aria-busy="true"] .subbar__link { animation: none; }
  .subbar__link:active { transform: none; }
}
```

### Markup Handoff Contract (for DEV_ENGINEER)

**DOM structure**
```html
<nav class="subbar" aria-label="Sections" data-scrolled="false" data-ready="false">
  <div class="subbar__track">
    <span class="subbar__pill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <a class="subbar__link" href="#SECTION_ID" aria-current="location">LABEL</a>
    <a class="subbar__link" href="#SECTION_ID_2">LABEL</a>
    <!-- optional: <span class="subbar__count">N</span> inside a link -->
  </div>
</nav>
<!-- each section heading: id="SECTION_ID" data-subbar-target -->
```

**Required hooks**

| Selector | Requirement |
|---|---|
| `nav.subbar` | Use a native `<nav>` with `aria-label`. |
| `.subbar__track` | Direct parent of the pill and the links. |
| `.subbar__pill` | Place it first in the track, with `aria-hidden="true"`. It holds no content. |
| `.subbar__link` | Use `<a href="#id">` (or `<button>` for non-anchor views). Exactly one link has `aria-current="location"` at a time. Use `page` for route tabs. |
| `[data-subbar-target]` | Put this on every section heading or section the bar links to. |
| `.subbar__empty` | Shown when there are no sections. |
| `.subbar__error` | Give it `role="alert"`, with a `.subbar__retry` button that re-runs the load. |
| `.subbar__count` | Optional, for tab counters. |

**`data-` and `aria-` hooks engineering must toggle**

| Hook | When to set it |
|---|---|
| `data-scrolled="true"` on `.subbar` | `scrollY` is greater than the bar's stuck offset, or when an `IntersectionObserver` sentinel above the bar leaves view. |
| `data-ready="true"` on `.subbar` | After the first pill measurement. Set it in a `requestAnimationFrame` so the pill does not slide in from 0. |
| `aria-busy="true"` on `.subbar` | While sections load. Keep the same number of links as the loaded state, with placeholder labels, so nothing shifts. |
| `aria-current` on `.subbar__link` | Move it to the tab for the section in view, using an `IntersectionObserver` or scroll-spy. Also move it on click. |
| `aria-disabled="true"` on a link | For unavailable sections. |

**CSS variables the JS must write**

These go on `.subbar__track` or `.subbar`.
- `--pill-x`: the active link's `offsetLeft`, in px (for example `"132px"`).
- `--pill-w`: the active link's `offsetWidth`, in px.
- Recompute on the active tab change, on `resize`, on `ResizeObserver` of the track, and after fonts load.
- Scroll the active link into view in the track with `scrollIntoView({inline:"center", block:"nearest"})`. Use `behavior:"auto"` under reduced motion.

**Optional**
- Set `--subbar-top` to the height of a fixed main header, for example `.subbar{--subbar-top:72px}`.

### States and keyboard
- **Default:** quiet muted text with a hairline border under the bar.
- **Hover:** stronger border and default text colour, with no layout shift.
- **Focus-visible:** 2px outline with a 2px offset, using `--color-border-focus`.
- **Active / selected:** `aria-current`, weight 500, and the sliding pill. Press gives a 1px tactile nudge.
- **Disabled:** 50% opacity.
- **Loading:** shimmer placeholders sized like the loaded tabs.
- **Empty and error:** the `.subbar__empty` and `.subbar__error` blocks above, with a Retry button in the error case.
- **Keyboard:** tabs are real links or buttons, so Tab and Enter work by default. No arrow-key roving is needed because this is a nav list, not a tablist.
- **Reduced motion:** the pill jumps to the new tab with no slide, and the shimmer stops. The selected state is still clear.

### Verification and open questions
- **Not run:** no browser check yet at 1440px or 390px, in light or dark, or under reduced motion, and no console check. Please have QA_AUDITOR run these after wiring: zero horizontal scroll, and the pill tracking the correct tab after resize.
- **Missing danger tokens:** `--color-danger-text` and `--color-danger-bg-subtle` are used with fallbacks, and the dark values are set locally. This is a UI-layer gap, so `design-system` should add them to the shared token set.
- **Pill width:** it animates both `transform` and `width`, as the skill's reference specifies. Width changes are limited to the small pill element. Switching to a `scaleX` pill would distort the corner radius.
- **Next skills:** hand the wired result to `a11y-audit` for a markup audit, and to `copy-tight` if the section labels need shortening.
